From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:05:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] iio: qcom_smgr: release the QMI handle through a void *
 wrapper

qcom_smgr_probe() hands qmi_handle_release() to devm_add_action_or_reset()
cast to void (*)(void *). With kCFI the indirect call through the cast
pointer fails the type check, so every unbind (the SLPI going down,
module removal, a probe failure after this point) oopses in
devm_action_release() and leaves the remoteproc lock held:

  CFI failure at devm_action_release+0x34/0x50
  (target: qmi_handle_release+0x0/0x18c [qmi_helpers]; expected type: 0x0ef81b7d)

Call it from a small wrapper with the right prototype instead.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index 1d5753bd2b..b2cebf9af0 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -732,6 +732,11 @@ static int qcom_smgr_register_sensor(struct qcom_smgr *smgr,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void qcom_smgr_qmi_release(void *data)
+{
+	qmi_handle_release(data);
+}
+
 static int qcom_smgr_probe(struct qrtr_device *qdev)
 {
 	struct qcom_smgr *smgr;
@@ -757,8 +762,7 @@ static int qcom_smgr_probe(struct qrtr_device *qdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(smgr->dev, ret,
 			"Failed to initialize sensor manager handle\n");
 
-	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(smgr->dev,
-				       (void(*)(void *))qmi_handle_release,
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(smgr->dev, qcom_smgr_qmi_release,
 				       &smgr->sns_smgr_hdl);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
